{#
   One article in a listing: its lead image, title, date, author, section, how
   long it takes to read, and the summary if there is one.

   The image is the part that was missing until feature 017. Every article in the
   fixtures has one, the CMS stores three sizes of each, and no listing showed
   any of them — a site that is entirely about publishing pictures and words was
   showing only the words.

   `thumbnail`, not the original: a listing of twelve articles would otherwise
   send twelve full-size photographs to render them two hundred pixels wide.

   Both the image and the summary are optional in the model, so the markup
   collapses rather than leaving a gap.
#}
<article class="border-b border-rule pb-8 last:border-0">
    <div class="flex gap-5">
        {% if article.featuredImage %}
            <a href="{{ path('article_show', { slug: article.slug }) }}"
               class="hidden shrink-0 sm:block"
               tabindex="-1"
               aria-hidden="true">
                <img src="{{ path('media_sized', { size: 'thumbnail', filename: article.featuredImage.filename }) }}"
                     alt=""
                     width="160"
                     height="107"
                     class="h-[107px] w-40 rounded object-cover"
                     loading="lazy"
                     data-hide-on-error>
            </a>
        {% endif %}

        <div class="min-w-0">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
                <a href="{{ path('article_show', { slug: article.slug }) }}"
                   class="text-ink no-underline hover:underline">
                    {{ article.title }}
                </a>
            </h2>

            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted">
                {% if article.publishedAt %}
                    <time datetime="{{ article.publishedAt|date('Y-m-d') }}">{{ article.publishedAt|date('j F Y') }}</time>
                    <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                {% endif %}
                {{ article.author.displayName }}
                {% if article.category %}
                    <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                    <a href="{{ path('category_show', { slug: article.category.slug }) }}" class="text-muted hover:text-ink">
                        {{ article.category.name }}
                    </a>
                {% endif %}
                <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                {{ article.content|reading_time }} min read
            </p>

            {% if article.excerpt %}
                <p class="mt-3 text-ink/80">{{ article.excerpt }}</p>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </div>
</article>
